# tela/spike/defects/d0-generic-alias-params.fab
# MINIMIZED REPRO — D0: a generic type alias does not bind its own type
# parameters (shared semantic layer; all targets).
#
# Before the fix: `type X<T> = T` fails with SEM008 unknown_type_name at the
# body `T`. The resolve pass lowers each alias body via `lower_type_expr`
# AFTER `resolve_stmt` has entered and exited the alias's module scope, so the
# alias's own SymbolKind::TypeParam symbols are out of scope during body
# lowering. AliasEntry carried only { def_id, ty, span }; the fix adds
# `type_params` and scopes them around the body lower (mirroring the HIR path
# hir/lower/decl.rs::lower_typus, which already push_type_params).
#
# Expected (all green, no SEM008):
#   - declaration `type X<T> = T`;
#   - usage `fn f(int x) → X<int> { return x }` typechecks with substitution
#     at use (Type::Applied(Alias, args) → substitute_type_params);
#   - the campaign sketch shape `type Nuntius<Message> = (Eventum) → Message`
#     checks green at declaration (en spelling; `typus` does not parse in the
#     en pack — recorded dialect divergence, not this unit).
#
# Removal predicate: the spike's inline function-type field
# `(Eventum) → Message` can revert to the alias form `Nuntius<Message>`.

type X<T> = T

class Eventum { }

type Nuntius<Message> = (Eventum) → Message

fn f(int x) → X<int> {
    return x
}
